<Project>

  <!-- Inherit the repository-wide settings, then add what only applies to shipping code. -->
  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove($(MSBuildThisFile), $(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..))" />

  <!--
    PLAN.md §4.2 decides the threading model up front: a map is single-threaded, and gameplay state
    is touched only from the tick that owns it. That invariant was documented and structural, but
    nothing enforced it — a future caller could reach for Task.Run and move game state onto a
    thread-pool thread, and the result would be a rare, unreproducible corruption rather than a
    failure anyone could trace back to the line that caused it.

    BannedSymbols.txt turns that into a build error. TreatWarningsAsErrors is already on, so RS0030
    fails the build rather than adding one more warning to scroll past.

    Tests are deliberately not covered: tests/Directory.Build.props imports the repository root
    directly, not this file, and driving a scheduler from a background task is exactly how you prove
    it is thread-safe.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.BannedApiAnalyzers" Version="4.14.0">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <AdditionalFiles Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)BannedSymbols.txt" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
